# Scoped to the eval-runner image only — the base and OPA gates must still fail
# on these CVEs. Loaded alongside the repo-root .trivyignore (shared accepted
# risks) via the trivyignores input in .github/workflows/build-eval-image.yml.

# CVE-2026-104851: fsspec RCE via crafted reference documents (HIGH)
# Fixed in fsspec 2026.6.0, but the version is capped by upstream pins:
# lightspeed-evaluation v0.8.0 requires datasets<=4.0.0, which requires
# fsspec<=2025.3.0 (even datasets 4.8.5 only allows <=2026.2.0; the cap is not
# lifted until datasets 5.x). fsspec is a transitive dep — eval-runner never
# imports it and never opens fsspec reference documents, so the attack vector
# is not exposed. Revisit when lightspeed-evaluation bumps its datasets pin.
CVE-2026-104851

# GHSA-g5ff-637f-6q2m: LiteLLM internal_user_viewer arbitrary local file read
# via vertex_ai_credentials (HIGH). Fixed in litellm 1.95.0, but
# lightspeed-evaluation v0.8.0 pins litellm>=1.84.0,<=1.89.3 so the fixed
# release cannot be installed. Eval-runner does not expose LiteLLM's
# internal_user_viewer / admin credential-upload APIs — it only uses the
# library as a model client through lightspeed-evaluation. Revisit when
# lightspeed-evaluation raises its litellm upper bound.
GHSA-g5ff-637f-6q2m
